Choosing a hosting provider for client websites isn't a decision we take lightly. We've looked at what's available and settled on Krystal for WordPress and custom-built sites — and there are clear reasons for that.

## Why Krystal

Krystal is a UK-based hosting provider with a strong reputation in the UK web industry. They're employee-owned, carbon-neutral, and have been consistently well-regarded for support quality and server performance.

For us, the important things are:

**UK-based infrastructure**: Servers in the UK mean faster load times for UK visitors — which is relevant for every client we work with, all of whom are based in or targeting the UK market.

**Reliable uptime**: Krystal's infrastructure is well-managed. We don't see the repeated downtime issues that come with oversold shared hosting.

**Good support**: When we need to resolve something at a server level, Krystal's support is responsive and technical. That matters when a client's site is down.

**Domains included**: We use Krystal to register and manage domains for clients too, keeping hosting and domain management in one place.

## Managed starter hosting is included

For managed starter websites, hosting, domain management, SSL, uptime monitoring, and security are included in the monthly plan. You do not need to choose a host or manage the technical setup yourself.

## Why hosting choice matters

The host you use affects load speeds, uptime reliability, support quality when things go wrong, and — indirectly — your Google rankings. [Read more about how hosting affects your rankings](/blog/does-your-website-host-affect-your-google-rankings/) or [find out what managed hosting with NC Digital includes](/services/website-hosting-security/).
